Subject: [PATCH] The specification API: contract field equations and the
 layout and record facts

User ruling (2026-10-16, G4's and B6 F3's escalations E1): consumers read specification-level
definitions through published equation lemmas, never by unfolding them.

- Contract/Basic, Contract/Seam: the data fields (pre, time, post, lo, hi) of Contract.trans,
  seq, inPhase and branch, by simps without the simp attribute.
- Contract/Catalog: the same for framedContract, every row contract (simps!), and the fields
  of the endpoint shapes seekPost and sweepPost.
- Catalog: joinFields_nil, joinFields_singleton, fieldsTape_of_nonneg, fieldsTape_of_neg,
  fieldsTape_of_length_le, fieldsTape_nil, fieldOffset_zero.
- CfgRecord: recordAt_iff; record_pos_lt public. RecordTable: recordLength_eq.

No statement changes; no simp lemma added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
